-- title:
--   Compatible integral sections of a finite free p-adic tower
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and write $\mathcal O$ for the integral closure of $\mathbb Z_p$ in `PadicAlgCl p`. Let $B : \mathbb N \to \mathrm{Type}$ be a family of commutative rings such that each $B_i$ is an algebra over $\mathcal O/\langle p^i\rangle$ which is finite and free as a module over it. Let $\rho_i : B_{i+1} \to B_i$ be ring homomorphisms which are compatible with the structure maps, in the sense that for every $x \in \mathcal O$ the element $\rho_i$ applied to the image of $x \bmod p^{i+1}$ in $B_{i+1}$ equals the image of $x \bmod p^i$ in $B_i$ (hypothesis `hρ`), which are surjective, and whose kernels are the principal ideals generated by the image in $B_{i+1}$ of $p^i \bmod p^{i+1}$. Let $\psi : B_1 \to \mathcal O/\sqrt{\langle p\rangle}$ be a ring homomorphism sending the image of $x \bmod p$ in $B_1$ to the class of $x$, for every $x \in \mathcal O$. Then there is a family of ring homomorphisms $\sigma_i : B_i \to \mathcal O/\langle p^i\rangle$ such that: each $\sigma_i$ is a section of the structure map $\mathcal O/\langle p^i\rangle \to B_i$; whenever $b \in B_{i+1}$ has $\sigma_{i+1}(b)$ equal to the class of some $x \in \mathcal O$, then $\sigma_i(\rho_i(b))$ is the class of $x$ modulo $p^i$; and $\sigma_1(b)$ is nilpotent for every $b \in B_1$ with $\psi(b) = 0$.
--
--   The tower $(B_i, \rho_i)$ is a finite flat formal scheme over $\mathrm{Spf}\,\mathcal O_{\mathbb C_p}$ and $\psi$ is a closed point of it; the statement produces an integral point, given by a compatible family of sections, lying over that closed point. It is the input to the divisibility of the group of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb C_p}$-valued points of a $p$-divisible group, used in [`PDivisibleGroup.exists_nsmul_eq_of_forall_isNilpotent_cpointsProj_one_of_isIntegral_iff`](thm.html#PDivisibleGroup.exists_nsmul_eq_of_forall_isNilpotent_cpointsProj_one_of_isIntegral_iff).
-- source:
